    <GaugingStation location="Tregony" name="Fal" number="48003">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Velocity area station augmented by a low flow side-contracted flume. Some data unreliable due to siltation of flume an inlet pipes.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Full range station with sound high flow measurement. Pre-digital rating missing and under investigation. One peak flow rating applied across period of record.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Originally a velocity-area station in a formalised trapezoidal channel built in 1961; augmented by a low flow, side-contracted flume 2.8m wide in 08/1967.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Data available from 06/1978, earlier data unreliable due to silting of inlet pipes. Data between 1967 and 1978 is unreliable due to siltation of the flume. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2020 (WINFAP Files v9) and in August 2025 (WINFAP Files v14).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Moderate modification to flows owing to industrial abstractions and returns.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Responsive catchment of moderate to low relief, draining Devonian slates, shales and grits. Upper reaches plateau-like alluvial flats. Traverses the kaolinised St Austell Granite. Land use is low grade agriculture and grazing, some woodland. No major changes to catchment.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">EI</Comment>
        </Comments>
